      "notes": "Handcrafted rejection: `before` is a drawing that carries content (the subset's committed DwgSnapshot, LibreDWG-cross-checked against the real architectural.dwg header), stamped AC1024 as every decoded drawing with content is; SetVersionInfo{version:\"AC1018\",maintenanceVersion:1,codepage:1252} asks this writer for R2004 object streams it does not lay out, so dispatch refuses it Fatal `mutation.invariant` (`written-as-ac1024`) and the drawing stays as it was. The AC1018 tree's mutation aggregate re-exports this exact leaf from AC1024 (`pub use crate::artifacts::dwg::standards::v_ac1024::subsets::any::schema::mutations::*`), so one real implementation backs both subsets."
